  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool reaches 0.591 accuracy, clearly above singleprofile PCA and multiprofile transformer, while image-only ResNet is weak. This suggests the next informative step is to test whether a learned RNA representation improves on PCA under the already-promising multiprofile avgpool setting. config_005 isolates the RNA encoder choice by changing only from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200, making it a focused exploitation of the current best direction and a useful check before adding multimodal fusion complexity."
